      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Okay, it seems like \"default\" does more than to just apply 5 default colors. It looks like it has more freedom in the means of giving things colors in different ways than you can do with the normal Color Palette.\n\nI get why this was done (to limit complexity), but it really limits us in terms of how we can use the UI colors. Cause due to this, there is no way to just for example tweak the default colors a bit, or to make a custom palette as good looking as default can be, due to us having less finer control.\n\nFor example, by default the fold out arrow and text relatively match in color as you can see on the first picture. This is not really possible with the new UI Themes, as we can't specifically give these drop downs a different color.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
